  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 350 AM EDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nThe long-term forecast indicates a pronounced ridge centered over \nthe Four Corners region, with an upper-level trough extending \nsouthward from the Midwest. This setup will push a front through \nthe area Saturday and usher in drier air through the day, with \ndewpoint temperatures dropping into the 50s to mid 60s across our \nCWA by Sunday afternoon. As such, expect mostly fair weather with \nslightly cooler mornings through the weekend into early next week,\nwith daytime high temperatures ranging from the upper 80s to low \n90s and lower RH values. \n\nA few stray showers or storms will be possible across the southern \nportion of our CWA Saturday afternoon; otherwise, the frontal \nboundary should come through mostly dry and bring an end to the \nprecipitation chances through Monday morning. By mid-week, the upper-\nlevel flow becomes more zonal, and conditions begin to favor the \ntypical diurnal thunderstorm and humid pattern we so often \nexperience during the month of August. As a result, we will need to \nkeep an eye on heat index values across the CWA during the second \nhalf of next week.",
